<title>SWEDEN: Denmark's Maersk orders two more Boeings.</title>
<headline>Denmark's Maersk orders two more Boeings.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's Maersk Air, which launched eight-times daily flights between Stockholm and Copenhagen on Monday in cooperation with Finnair, said it ordered two new Boeing 737-500 SP jets, bringing the total number of such planes ordered to 13.  </p>
<p>Maersk said it had also ordered 12 of the newest member of the 737 family, the 700 series. The airline is due to be the first to take delivery of the new series when two are delivered in November.</p>
<p>Maersk said it had sold two older 737-500s to foreign buyers. -- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
</text>
